        <td style="padding:10px 12px;font-weight:700;color:#374151;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;vertical-align:top;width:36px;">20</td>
        <td style="padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;vertical-align:top;">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#111827;margin-bottom:6px;">Which target is appropriate for preserving the client source IP in common NLB designs?</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:4px;"><strong>Your Answer:</strong> <span style="color:#dc2626">A Route 53 hosted zone target</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:4px;"><strong>Correct Answer:</strong> <span style="color:#059669">Targets reached through NLB transport-layer forwarding with the relevant target settings</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;background:#eff6ff;border-left:3px solid #4f46e5;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;color:#1e3a8a;margin-top:6px;"><strong>💡 Explanation:</strong> NLB is designed for transport-layer forwarding and supports client-IP preservation behavior depending on target type and protocol.</div>
        </td>
        <td style="padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap;font-weight:700;font-size:12px;color:#dc2626">❌ Wrong</td>
