        <td style="padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;vertical-align:top;">
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#111827;margin-bottom:6px;">Transit Gateway route tables can segment attachments into isolated routing domains.</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:4px;"><strong>Your Answer:</strong> <span style="color:#059669">True</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:4px;"><strong>Correct Answer:</strong> <span style="color:#059669">True</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;background:#eff6ff;border-left:3px solid #4f46e5;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;color:#1e3a8a;margin-top:6px;"><strong>💡 Explanation:</strong> Attachments can associate with one route table and propagate routes to selected route tables, supporting segmentation such as production and non-production.</div>
        </td>
        <td style="padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap;font-weight:700;font-size:12px;color:#059669">✅ Correct</td>
