          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#111827;margin-bottom:6px;">What is a safer SSH rule than allowing TCP 22 from 0.0.0.0/0?</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:4px;"><strong>Your Answer:</strong> <span style="color:#059669">Allow TCP 22 only from an approved administrator CIDR or controlled access path</span></div>
